ed-super-block-optimizations-averaged-a-1-15-s--e5d7486c0e56\",\n        \"claim-the-profile-based-transformations-controlled-executable-size-growth-averaging-1--5bacab4b8a28\",\n        \"claim-the-experiments-used-separate-profiling-inputs-and-performance-measurement-input--ee5ac2fa5a94\",\n        \"claim-the-implementation-cost-of-profile-based-classic-optimization-was-modest-relativ--062df22ec16c\",\n        \"claim-direct-prediction-of-the-best-compiler-option-is-practical-for-relatively-small--fe68da808ef3\",\n        \"claim-thread-coarsening-decisions-are-context-dependent-because-coarsening-can-improve--4878860bda89\",\n        \"claim-machine-learning-based-compiler-optimization-is-limited-by-the-quality-represent--f9c7d385cc26\",\n        \"claim-the-major-effectiveness-mechanisms-are-eliminating-entries-into-the-middle-of-tr--4bc0ff5e21b0\",\n        \"claim-remote-cnot-execution-consumes-bell-state-resources-and-is-limited-by-the-number--ff11e4d2be8e\",\n        \"claim-in-the-worst-case-topology-the-entanglement-swapping-based-strategy-has-per-laye--bd58d42b2d90\",\n        \"claim-the-data-qubit-swapping-based-strategy-arranges-data-qubits-so-each-cnot-in-a-la--ba4ebf62d172\",\n        \"claim-the-proposed-compiler-is-computationally-efficient-because-distributing-a-circui--b9f318c6234c\",\n        \"claim-experimental-validation-on-medium-size-quantum-circuits-respected-the-analytical--82f1bfd54f5c\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"claims\": [\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-classic-scalar-optimizations-can-be-reformulated-to-operate-on-super-blocks-and--79ce55378df0\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Classic optimizations fit super-blocks\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-01-using-profile-information-to-assist-classic-code-optimizations--219edcf6f0cf\",\n      \"text\": \"Classic scalar optimizations can be reformulated to operate on super-blocks and super-block loops rather than only on traditional basic blocks or whole loops.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-direct-prediction-of-the-best-compiler-option-is-practical-for-relatively-small--fe68da808ef3\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Constrained choices enable direct prediction\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-02-machine-learning-in-compiler-optimization--5fbaa9c3f69d\",\n      \"text\": \"Direct prediction of the best compiler option is practical for relatively small optimization problems and has produced measurable gains in loop unrolling and thread-coarsening studies.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-distributed-quantum-compilers-must-model-temporal-coupling-map-dynamics-because--0883f72a302d\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Coupling maps become dynamic\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-03-compiler-design-for-distributed-quantum-computing--64a02810764d\",\n      \"text\": \"Distributed quantum compilers must model temporal coupling-map dynamics because remote operations are constrained by Bell-state availability, Bell-state regeneration, and classical communication latency.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-distributed-quantum-computing-can-let-remote-quantum-processing-units-cooperate--c8a669f6488f\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Distributed QPUs cooperate virtually\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-03-compiler-design-for-distributed-quantum-computing--64a02810764d\",\n      \"text\": \"Distributed quantum computing can let remote quantum processing units cooperate as a virtual quantum processor for tasks that individual noisy intermediate-scale quantum devices cannot handle alone.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-distributed-quantum-computing-requires-compilers-that-can-map-arbitrary-quantum--e4ea92cd41cd\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Distributed architectures require compilers\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-03-compiler-design-for-distributed-quantum-computing--64a02810764d\",\n      \"text\": \"Distributed quantum computing requires compilers that can map arbitrary quantum algorithms to distributed architectures while accounting for network and communication constraints.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-effective-concentration-calibration-guides-thresholds--367a566abb69\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Calibration guides gate thresholds\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-05-compiler-aided-systematic-construction-of-large-scale-dna-strand-displacement-circuits--367a566abb69\",\n      \"text\": \"Effective concentration calibration provides quantitative threshold choices that restore desired OR and AND gate behavior for unpurified seesaw components.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-entanglement-swapping-augments-distributed-processor-connectivity-by-enabling-re--b0cac39f5fb5\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Entanglement swapping augments connectivity\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-03-compiler-design-for-distributed-quantum-computing--64a02810764d\",\n      \"text\": \"Entanglement swapping augments distributed-processor connectivity by enabling remote CNOTs between processors that are not directly connected by a quantum link, but it increases EPR-pair consumption at intermediate processors.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-execution-profiles-integrated-into-an-optimizing-c-compiler-can-guide-classic-op--20be52b7603e\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Profiles guide classic optimizations\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-01-using-profile-information-to-assist-classic-code-optimizations--219edcf6f0cf\",\n      \"text\": \"Execution profiles integrated into an optimizing C compiler can guide classic optimizations toward the program regions that run most often.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-experimental-validation-on-medium-size-quantum-circuits-respected-the-analytical--82f1bfd54f5c\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Experiments respect analytical bounds\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-03-compiler-design-for-distributed-quantum-computing--64a02810764d\",\n      \"text\": \"Experimental validation on medium-size quantum circuits respected the analytical bounds, and the data-qubit-swapping strategy generally required fewer link-generation layers and lower circuit depth than entanglement swapping alone.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-feature-selection-and-dimension-reduction-are-necessary-in-compiler-learning-pro--ecd12a4a4f1f\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Feature reduction preserves signal\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-02-machine-learning-in-compiler-optimization--5fbaa9c3f69d\",\n      \"text\": \"Feature selection and dimension reduction are necessary in compiler-learning problems because larger feature spaces require more training examples and can contain redundant information.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-full-circuit-recovers-ideal-ca-patterns--367a566abb69\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Outputs match automata patterns\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-05-compiler-aided-systematic-construction-of-large-scale-dna-strand-displacement-circuits--367a566abb69\",\n      \"text\": \"The full rule 110-124 DNA circuit produced dual-rail fluorescence outputs at 24 hours that visually matched the intended cellular automata pattern relationships.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-future-research-in-machine-learning-compilation-extends-beyond-choosing-optimiza--faf587f1fc17\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Open questions extend beyond optimization\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-02-machine-learning-in-compiler-optimization--5fbaa9c3f69d\",\n      \"text\": \"Future research in machine-learning compilation extends beyond choosing optimizations to mapping program and hardware spaces, learning analyses, discovering common features, and possibly learning better intermediate representations.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-ilp-based-code-scratchpad-allocation-lowers-wcet-by-moving-beneficial-basic-bloc--d5d88da4e90e\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Code SPM reduces WCET\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-04-a-compiler-framework-for-the-reduction-of-worst-case-execution-times--5aee9841160e\",\n      \"text\": \"ILP-based code scratchpad allocation lowers WCET by moving beneficial basic-block regions into fast program scratchpad memory with negligible code-size and solver overhead.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-ilp-based-data-scratchpad-allocation-lowers-wcet-by-moving-frequently-accessed-v--8ceca90523fc\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Data SPM reduces WCET\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-04-a-compiler-framework-for-the-reduction-of-worst-case-execution-times--5aee9841160e\",\n      \"text\": \"ILP-based data scratchpad allocation lowers WCET by moving frequently accessed variables into fast data scratchpad memory without changing generated code size.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-in-the-worst-case-topology-the-entanglement-swapping-based-strategy-has-per-laye--bd58d42b2d90\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Entanglement strategy has linear bound\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-03-compiler-design-for-distributed-quantum-computing--64a02810764d\",\n      \"text\": \"In the worst-case topology, the entanglement-swapping-based strategy has per-layer depth overhead bounded by n/2 times a hardware-dependent constant des, where des equals cle plus cbsm plus ccx.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-interprocedural-slicing-and-polyhedral-loop-evaluation-substantially-reduce-loop--8f361a6ac310\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Slicing accelerates loop analysis\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-04-a-compiler-framework-for-the-reduction-of-worst-case-execution-times--5aee9841160e\",\n      \"text\": \"Interprocedural slicing and polyhedral loop evaluation substantially reduce loop-analysis time for many benchmarks while preserving safe loop-bound analysis.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-machine-learning-based-compilation-can-make-compiler-optimization-more-evidence--20aeeff3a32c\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Empirical workflows improve compiler evidence\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-02-machine-learning-in-compiler-optimization--5fbaa9c3f69d\",\n      \"text\": \"Machine-learning-based compilation can make compiler optimization more evidence based because models must be grounded in empirical data that can be tested and independently scrutinized.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-machine-learning-based-compilation-can-use-a-model-inside-the-compiler-to-choose--f8131a5c483d\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Learning guides compiler choices\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-02-machine-learning-in-compiler-optimization--5fbaa9c3f69d\",\n      \"text\": \"Machine-learning-based compilation can use a model inside the compiler to choose compiler heuristics or optimizations for a given program according to learned evidence about what makes code faster, smaller, or less power hungry.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-machine-learning-based-compiler-optimization-is-limited-by-the-quality-represent--f9c7d385cc26\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Training data limits learning\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-02-machine-learning-in-compiler-optimization--5fbaa9c3f69d\",\n      \"text\": \"Machine-learning-based compiler optimization is limited by the quality, representativeness, and cost of its training data and cannot by itself create legal transformations or derive legality analyses.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-on-the-benchmark-suite-profile-based-super-block-optimizations-averaged-a-1-15-s--e5d7486c0e56\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Profile optimization speeds benchmarks\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-01-using-profile-information-to-assist-classic-code-optimizations--219edcf6f0cf\",\n      \"text\": \"On the benchmark suite, profile-based super-block optimizations averaged a 1.15 speedup over the prototype compiler's globally optimized code.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-outlier-gates-expose-synthesis-variation--367a566abb69\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Outliers disrupt gate composition\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-05-compiler-aided-systematic-construction-of-large-scale-dna-strand-displacement-circuits--367a566abb69\",\n      \"text\": \"Gate calibration can identify outlier unpurified components whose effective concentrations differ enough to disrupt multi-layer circuit composition.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-profile-based-classic-optimizations-are-intended-to-complement-conventional-opti--6bcefbcf9607\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Profile optimizations complement convention\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-01-using-profile-information-to-assist-classic-code-optimizations--219edcf6f0cf\",\n      \"text\": \"Profile-based classic optimizations are intended to complement conventional optimizations rather than replace them.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-program-features-provide-the-quantifiable-representation-that-allows-learning-al--a254f7b701be\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Features encode program behavior\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-02-machine-learning-in-compiler-optimization--5fbaa9c3f69d\",\n      \"text\": \"Program features provide the quantifiable representation that allows learning algorithms to reason about source code, intermediate representation, runtime profiles, or combinations of those properties.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-remote-cnot-execution-consumes-bell-state-resources-and-is-limited-by-the-number--ff11e4d2be8e\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Remote CNOTs consume Bell states\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-03-compiler-design-for-distributed-quantum-computing--64a02810764d\",\n      \"text\": \"Remote CNOT execution consumes Bell-state resources and is limited by the number of available communication qubits, creating a tradeoff between communication capacity and data-qubit capacity.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-rule-110-124-circuit-has-78-species--367a566abb69\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Circuit has 78 species\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-05-compiler-aided-systematic-construction-of-large-scale-dna-strand-displacement-circuits--367a566abb69\",\n      \"text\": \"The compiled rule 110-124 DNA strand displacement circuit contains six layers and 78 distinct initial DNA species.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-seesaw-compiler-automates-dna-circuit-design--367a566abb69\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Compiler automates DNA circuits\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-05-compiler-aided-systematic-construction-of-large-scale-dna-strand-displacement-circuits--367a566abb69\",\n      \"text\": \"The Seesaw Compiler automates the translation of feedforward digital logic into equivalent dual-rail and seesaw DNA strand displacement circuits, while producing simulation code and DNA sequences for construction.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-signal-restoration-compensates-for-impurity--367a566abb69\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Restoration compensates impurity\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-05-compiler-aided-systematic-construction-of-large-scale-dna-strand-displacement-circuits--367a566abb69\",\n      \"text\": \"Signal restoration and component tuning compensate for impurity in unpurified seesaw circuits, although leak reactions and sensitivity to synthesis and stoichiometry errors remain limiting concerns.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-static-wcet-reduction-depends-on-optimizing-the-worst-case-execution-path-becaus--b6a70fae6e3d\",\n      \"short_title\": \"WCEP governs WCET savings\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-04-a-compiler-framework-for-the-reduction-of-worst-case-execution-times--5aee9841160e\",\n      \"text\": \"Static WCET reduction depends on optimizing the worst-case execution path, because reducing a noncritical path or a local block can leave the global WCET unchanged or only partly reduced.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-super-blocks-represent-frequently-executed-paths-as-linear-basic-block-sequences--7bbb510c9bb0\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Super-blocks isolate hot paths\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-01-using-profile-information-to-assist-classic-code-optimizations--219edcf6f0cf\",\n      \"text\": \"Super-blocks represent frequently executed paths as linear basic-block sequences that can only be entered at the first block but may exit from any block.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-supervised-learning-for-compiler-optimization-learns-correlations-between-progra--217abf25c992\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Supervision maps features to decisions\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-02-machine-learning-in-compiler-optimization--5fbaa9c3f69d\",\n      \"text\": \"Supervised learning for compiler optimization learns correlations between program-feature values and the optimization decisions that produce optimal or near-optimal empirical performance.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-synthesis-error-model-explains-delayed-outputs--367a566abb69\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Error model explains delay\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-05-compiler-aided-systematic-construction-of-large-scale-dna-strand-displacement-circuits--367a566abb69\",\n      \"text\": \"A model that represents synthesis errors in unpurified molecules predicts the slower 24-hour behavior of the rule 110-124 circuit better than the purified-circuit model.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-systematic-flow-shortens-unpurified-circuit-building--367a566abb69\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Procedure shortens circuit building\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-05-compiler-aided-systematic-construction-of-large-scale-dna-strand-displacement-circuits--367a566abb69\",\n      \"text\": \"A three-step systematic procedure of calibration, outlier adjustment, and output tuning enabled construction of the rule 110 sub-circuit in three days.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-tail-duplication-creates-additional-optimization-opportunities-because-it-can-ma--6c81300e0307\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Duplication exposes producer relationships\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-01-using-profile-information-to-assist-classic-code-optimizations--219edcf6f0cf\",\n      \"text\": \"Tail duplication creates additional optimization opportunities because it can make an earlier operation the sole producer of operands used later in a hot path.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-the-data-qubit-swapping-based-strategy-arranges-data-qubits-so-each-cnot-in-a-la--ba4ebf62d172\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Data swapping lowers asymptotic overhead\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-03-compiler-design-for-distributed-quantum-computing--64a02810764d\",\n      \"text\": \"The data-qubit-swapping-based strategy arranges data qubits so each CNOT in a layer operates on neighboring processors, and its compiled per-layer depth does not exceed n/4 dqs plus dqs prime.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-the-experiments-used-separate-profiling-inputs-and-performance-measurement-input--ee5ac2fa5a94\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Benchmarks use separate inputs\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-01-using-profile-information-to-assist-classic-code-optimizations--219edcf6f0cf\",\n      \"text\": \"The experiments used separate profiling inputs and performance-measurement inputs across realistic C application programs.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-the-implementation-cost-of-profile-based-classic-optimization-was-modest-relativ--062df22ec16c\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Implementation cost is modest\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-01-using-profile-information-to-assist-classic-code-optimizations--219edcf6f0cf\",\n      \"text\": \"The implementation cost of profile-based classic optimization was modest relative to the existing global optimizer.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-the-machine-learning-compiler-workflow-separates-model-learning-from-deployment--a04ee1ab9738\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Training precedes deployment\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-02-machine-learning-in-compiler-optimization--5fbaa9c3f69d\",\n      \"text\": \"The machine-learning compiler workflow separates model learning from deployment: training data is used to learn a model, and the learned model is then inserted into the compiler to make predictions for new programs.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-the-major-effectiveness-mechanisms-are-eliminating-entries-into-the-middle-of-tr--4bc0ff5e21b0\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Effectiveness has two mechanisms\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-01-using-profile-information-to-assist-classic-code-optimizations--219edcf6f0cf\",\n      \"text\": \"The major effectiveness mechanisms are eliminating entries into the middle of traces and optimizing the most frequently executed loop path.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-the-paper-s-worst-case-system-model-uses-one-data-qubit-per-processor-and-a-one--9e5973bc3485\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Worst case maximizes overhead\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-03-compiler-design-for-distributed-quantum-computing--64a02810764d\",\n      \"text\": \"The paper's worst-case system model uses one data qubit per processor and a one-dimensional nearest-neighbor processor topology, making every CNOT remote and maximizing distributed-computation overhead.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-the-profile-based-transformations-controlled-executable-size-growth-averaging-1--5bacab4b8a28\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Code expansion stays controlled\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-01-using-profile-information-to-assist-classic-code-optimizations--219edcf6f0cf\",\n      \"text\": \"The profile-based transformations controlled executable size growth, averaging 1.07 relative size compared with globally optimized programs.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-the-proposed-compiler-is-computationally-efficient-because-distributing-a-circui--b9f318c6234c\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Compiler complexity is polynomial\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-03-compiler-design-for-distributed-quantum-computing--64a02810764d\",\n      \"text\": \"The proposed compiler is computationally efficient because distributing a circuit has O(d n squared) complexity, with d the circuit depth and n the number of QPUs or logical qubits in the modeled worst case.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-the-wcc-optimizations-compose-applying-register-allocation-code-and-data-scratch--1393cb5b3616\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Optimizations compose strongly\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-04-a-compiler-framework-for-the-reduction-of-worst-case-execution-times--5aee9841160e\",\n      \"text\": \"The WCC optimizations compose: applying register allocation, code and data scratchpad allocation, and procedure positioning to matmult reduces WCET by more than 70 percent relative to WCC -O2.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-thread-coarsening-decisions-are-context-dependent-because-coarsening-can-improve--4878860bda89\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Thread coarsening is context dependent\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-02-machine-learning-in-compiler-optimization--5fbaa9c3f69d\",\n      \"text\": \"Thread coarsening decisions are context dependent because coarsening can improve instruction-level parallelism and memory behavior while also reducing parallelism or increasing register pressure on particular programs and hardware.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-trace-selection-followed-by-tail-duplication-converts-frequently-executed-traces--1483ee9d0534\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Tail duplication forms super-blocks\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-01-using-profile-information-to-assist-classic-code-optimizations--219edcf6f0cf\",\n      \"text\": \"Trace selection followed by tail duplication converts frequently executed traces into super-blocks by removing control-flow entries into the middle of a trace.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-unpurified-strands-can-build-complex-circuits--367a566abb69\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Unpurified strands support circuits\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-05-compiler-aided-systematic-construction-of-large-scale-dna-strand-displacement-circuits--367a566abb69\",\n      \"text\": \"Unpurified DNA strands can be used to construct complex DNA strand displacement circuits when circuit design software is combined with simplified experimental procedures.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-wcc-couples-a-c-compiler-to-the-ait-static-wcet-analyzer-so-that-wcet-data-is-pr--13f9763eb2a9\",\n      \"short_title\": \"WCC integrates static analysis\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-04-a-compiler-framework-for-the-reduction-of-worst-case-execution-times--5aee9841160e\",\n      \"text\": \"WCC couples a C compiler to the aiT static WCET analyzer so that WCET data is produced transparently during compilation rather than by a separate manual post-compilation step.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-wcc-s-back-annotation-raises-assembly-level-wcet-information-to-source-level-icd--fc00d3acd6de\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Back annotation enables optimization\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-04-a-compiler-framework-for-the-reduction-of-worst-case-execution-times--5aee9841160e\",\n      \"text\": \"WCC’s back-annotation raises assembly-level WCET information to source-level ICD-C structures, enabling source-level optimizations to use WCET, WCEP membership, execution frequencies, cache misses, code size, and spill-code data.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-wcc-s-loop-analyzer-computes-safe-loop-iteration-bounds-for-most-benchmark-loops--5eb419e33259\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Loop bounds become automatic\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-04-a-compiler-framework-for-the-reduction-of-worst-case-execution-times--5aee9841160e\",\n      \"text\": \"WCC’s loop analyzer computes safe loop iteration bounds for most benchmark loops and exact bounds for the great majority, reducing reliance on manual flow facts.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-wcet-aware-procedure-cloning-improves-wcet-estimates-by-specializing-functions-w--808a9c5da846\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Cloning sharpens loop bounds\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-04-a-compiler-framework-for-the-reduction-of-worst-case-execution-times--5aee9841160e\",\n      \"text\": \"WCET-aware procedure cloning improves WCET estimates by specializing functions whose data-dependent loop bounds become constant in cloned calling contexts, but it trades timing precision for code-size growth.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-wcet-aware-register-allocation-lowers-wcet-by-avoiding-spill-code-on-the-wcep-ev--a21ac879b656\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Register allocation protects WCEP\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-04-a-compiler-framework-for-the-reduction-of-worst-case-execution-times--5aee9841160e\",\n      \"text\": \"WCET-aware register allocation lowers WCET by avoiding spill code on the WCEP, even when this increases total spill code or text size outside the critical path.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-wcet-centric-procedure-positioning-reduces-instruction-cache-conflict-misses-by--47eeb6643a90\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Positioning reduces cache misses\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-04-a-compiler-framework-for-the-reduction-of-worst-case-execution-times--5aee9841160e\",\n      \"text\": \"WCET-centric procedure positioning reduces instruction-cache conflict misses by reordering functions using static WCET-derived call frequencies rather than profiling input data.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-weighted-flow-graphs-expose-hot-paths-by-attaching-execution-counts-to-basic-blo--49c47f8431d5\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Weighted graphs expose hot paths\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-01-using-profile-information-to-assist-classic-code-optimizations--219edcf6f0cf\",\n      \"text\": \"Weighted flow graphs expose hot paths by attaching execution counts to basic blocks and taken counts to control-flow arcs.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"relations\": [\n    {\n      \"relation_id\": \"derived_from:claim-future-research-in-machine-learning-compilation-extends-beyond-choosing-optimiza--faf587f1fc17->claim-machine-learning-based-compilation-can-make-compiler-optimization-more-evidence--20aeeff3a32c\",\n      \"relation_type\": \"derived_from\",\n      \"source_claim_id\": null,\n      \"target_claim_id\": null,\n      \"rationale\": \"The future research agenda follows from treating compiler optimization as an empirical learning problem.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"relation_id\": \"derived_from:claim-the-data-qubit-swapping-based-strategy-arranges-data-qubits-so-each-cnot-in-a-la--ba4ebf62d172->claim-the-proposed-compiler-is-computationally-efficient-because-distributing-a-circui--b9f318c6234c\",\n      \"relation_type\": \"derived_from\",\n      \"source_claim_id\": null,\n      \"target_claim_id\": null,\n      \"rationale\": \"The data-qubit-swapping theorem contributes to the compiler's polynomial effectiveness and complexity profile.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"relation_id\": \"derived_from:claim-trace-selection-followed-by-tail-duplication-converts-frequently-executed-traces--1483ee9d0534->claim-super-blocks-represent-frequently-executed-paths-as-linear-basic-block-sequences--7bbb510c9bb0\",\n      \"relation_type\": \"derived_from\",\n      \"source_claim_id\": null,\n      \"target_claim_id\": null,\n      \"rationale\": \"Trace selection and tail duplication are the construction steps that enforce the entry property of super-blocks.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"relation_id\": \"derived_from:claim-wcc-s-back-annotation-raises-assembly-level-wcet-information-to-source-level-icd--fc00d3acd6de->claim-wcet-aware-procedure-cloning-improves-wcet-estimates-by-specializing-functions-w--808a9c5da846\",\n      \"relation_type\": \"derived_from\",\n      \"source_claim_id\": null,\n      \"target_claim_id\": null,\n      \"rationale\": \"WCET-aware cloning relies on back-annotated timing and loop-context information to select profitable source-level clones.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"relation_id\": \"derived_from:claim-wcc-s-back-annotation-raises-assembly-level-wcet-information-to-source-level-icd--fc00d3acd6de->claim-wcet-centric-procedure-positioning-reduces-instruction-cache-conflict-misses-by--47eeb6643a90\",\n      \"relation_type\": \"derived_from\",\n      \"source_claim_id\": null,\n      \"target_claim_id\": null,\n      \"rationale\": \"WCET-centric procedure positioning depends on back-annotated call frequencies and cache-related timing data.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"relation_id\": \"similar:claim-execution-profiles-integrated-into-an-optimizing-c-compiler-can-guide-classic-op--20be52b7603e|claim-profile-based-classic-optimizations-are-intended-to-complement-conventional-opti--6bcefbcf9607\",\n      \"relation_type\": \"similar\",\n      \"source_claim_id\": null,\n      \"target_claim_id\": null,\n      \"rationale\": \"Both claims frame profile-based optimization as an addition to, rather than a replacement for, conventional optimization.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"relation_id\": \"supports:claim-effective-concentration-calibration-guides-thresholds--367a566abb69->claim-unpurified-strands-can-build-complex-circuits--367a566abb69\",\n      \"relation_type\": \"supports\",\n      \"source_claim_id\": null,\n      \"target_claim_id\": null,\n      \"rationale\": \"Calibrated thresholds explain how unpurified components can still produce desired gate behavior.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"relation_id\": \"supports:claim-experimental-validation-on-medium-size-quantum-circuits-respected-the-analytical--82f1bfd54f5c->claim-in-the-worst-case-topology-the-entanglement-swapping-based-strategy-has-per-laye--bd58d42b2d90\",\n      \"relation_type\": \"supports\",\n      \"source_claim_id\": null,\n      \"target_claim_id\": null,\n      \"rationale\": \"The validation table reports that the analytical upper bounds hold across the evaluated benchmark circuits.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"relation_id\": \"supports:claim-experimental-validation-on-medium-size-quantum-circuits-respected-the-analytical--82f1bfd54f5c->claim-the-data-qubit-swapping-based-strategy-arranges-data-qubits-so-each-cnot-in-a-la--ba4ebf62d172\",\n      \"relation_type\": \"supports\",\n      \"source_claim_id\": null,\n      \"target_claim_id\": null,\n      \"rationale\": \"The comparative figures support the practical value of the data-qubit-swapping strategy relative to entanglement swapping alone.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"relation_id\": \"supports:claim-feature-selection-and-dimension-reduction-are-necessary-in-compiler-learning-pro--ecd12a4a4f1f->claim-supervised-learning-for-compiler-optimization-learns-correlations-between-progra--217abf25c992\",\n      \"relation_type\": \"supports\",\n      \"source_claim_id\": null,\n      \"target_claim_id\": null,\n      \"rationale\": \"Feature reduction improves the feasibility of supervised mapping from program descriptions to decisions.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"relation_id\": \"supports:claim-ilp-based-code-scratchpad-allocation-lowers-wcet-by-moving-beneficial-basic-bloc--d5d88da4e90e->claim-the-wcc-optimizations-compose-applying-register-allocation-code-and-data-scratch--1393cb5b3616\",\n      \"relation_type\": \"supports\",\n      \"source_claim_id\": null,\n      \"target_claim_id\": null,\n      \"rationale\": \"Code scratchpad allocation contributes one of the measured components in the combined matmult WCET reduction.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"relation_id\": \"supports:claim-ilp-based-data-scratchpad-allocation-lowers-wcet-by-moving-frequently-accessed-v--8ceca90523fc->claim-the-wcc-optimizations-compose-applying-register-allocation-code-and-data-scratch--1393cb5b3616\",\n      \"relation_type\": \"supports\",\n      \"source_claim_id\": null,\n      \"target_claim_id\": null,\n      \"rationale\": \"Data scratchpad allocation contributes another measured component in the combined matmult WCET reduction.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"relation_id\": \"supports:claim-machine-learning-based-compiler-optimization-is-limited-by-the-quality-represent--f9c7d385cc26->claim-machine-learning-based-compilation-can-make-compiler-optimization-more-evidence--20aeeff3a32c\",\n      \"relation_type\": \"supports\",\n      \"source_claim_id\": null,\n      \"target_claim_id\": null,\n      \"rationale\": \"The limits on training data and legality make empirical scrutiny necessary rather than optional.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"relation_id\": \"supports:claim-on-the-benchmark-suite-profile-based-super-block-optimizations-averaged-a-1-15-s--e5d7486c0e56->claim-execution-profiles-integrated-into-an-optimizing-c-compiler-can-guide-classic-op--20be52b7603e\",\n      \"relation_type\": \"supports\",\n      \"source_claim_id\": null,\n      \"target_claim_id\": null,\n      \"rationale\": \"The measured benchmark speedups support the usefulness of integrating profile information into classic optimizations.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"relation_id\": \"supports:claim-outlier-gates-expose-synthesis-variation--367a566abb69->claim-systematic-flow-shortens-unpurified-circuit-building--367a566abb69\",\n      \"relation_type\": \"supports\",\n      \"source_claim_id\": null,\n      \"target_claim_id\": null,\n      \"rationale\": \"Measured outlier gate ratios justify the procedure’s outlier-identification and adjustment step.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"relation_id\": \"supports:claim-program-features-provide-the-quantifiable-representation-that-allows-learning-al--a254f7b701be->claim-the-machine-learning-compiler-workflow-separates-model-learning-from-deployment--a04ee1ab9738\",\n      \"relation_type\": \"supports\",\n      \"source_claim_id\": null,\n      \"target_claim_id\": null,\n      \"rationale\": \"Feature representations are required for the training stage that precedes deployment.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"relation_id\": \"supports:claim-remote-cnot-execution-consumes-bell-state-resources-and-is-limited-by-the-number--ff11e4d2be8e->claim-distributed-quantum-compilers-must-model-temporal-coupling-map-dynamics-because--0883f72a302d\",\n      \"relation_type\": \"supports\",\n      \"source_claim_id\": null,\n      \"target_claim_id\": null,\n      \"rationale\": \"Bell-state consumption and communication-qubit limits are the resource dynamics that require distributed coupling maps to become temporal rather than static.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"relation_id\": \"supports:claim-rule-110-124-circuit-has-78-species--367a566abb69->claim-unpurified-strands-can-build-complex-circuits--367a566abb69\",\n      \"relation_type\": \"supports\",\n      \"source_claim_id\": null,\n      \"target_claim_id\": null,\n      \"rationale\": \"The six-layer, 78-species implementation is the concrete case demonstrating complex circuits from unpurified strands.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"relation_id\": \"supports:claim-signal-restoration-compensates-for-impurity--367a566abb69->claim-unpurified-strands-can-build-complex-circuits--367a566abb69\",\n      \"relation_type\": \"supports\",\n      \"source_claim_id\": null,\n      \"target_claim_id\": null,\n      \"rationale\": \"Signal restoration and tuning provide the compensatory mechanism that makes unpurified construction feasible.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"relation_id\": \"supports:claim-static-wcet-reduction-depends-on-optimizing-the-worst-case-execution-path-becaus--b6a70fae6e3d->claim-wcc-couples-a-c-compiler-to-the-ait-static-wcet-analyzer-so-that-wcet-data-is-pr--13f9763eb2a9\",\n      \"relation_type\": \"supports\",\n      \"source_claim_id\": null,\n      \"target_claim_id\": null,\n      \"rationale\": \"The need to optimize the WCEP explains why WCC integrates static WCET analysis into compilation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"relation_id\": \"supports:claim-synthesis-error-model-explains-delayed-outputs--367a566abb69->claim-full-circuit-recovers-ideal-ca-patterns--367a566abb69\",\n      \"relation_type\": \"supports\",\n      \"source_claim_id\": null,\n      \"target_claim_id\": null,\n      \"rationale\": \"The unpurified synthesis-error model explains why the successful full-circuit readout occurs on a slower 24-hour timescale.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"relation_id\": \"supports:claim-systematic-flow-shortens-unpurified-circuit-building--367a566abb69->claim-full-circuit-recovers-ideal-ca-patterns--367a566abb69\",\n      \"relation_type\": \"supports\",\n      \"source_claim_id\": null,\n      \"target_claim_id\": null,\n      \"rationale\": \"The systematic build procedure leads into the full circuit implementation evaluated at 24 hours.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"relation_id\": \"supports:claim-tail-duplication-creates-additional-optimization-opportunities-because-it-can-ma--6c81300e0307->claim-classic-scalar-optimizations-can-be-reformulated-to-operate-on-super-blocks-and--79ce55378df0\",\n      \"relation_type\": \"supports\",\n      \"source_claim_id\": null,\n      \"target_claim_id\": null,\n      \"rationale\": \"The operation-combining example explains why super-block scope exposes more opportunities for classic optimizations.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"relation_id\": \"supports:claim-the-machine-learning-compiler-workflow-separates-model-learning-from-deployment--a04ee1ab9738->claim-machine-learning-based-compilation-can-use-a-model-inside-the-compiler-to-choose--f8131a5c483d\",\n      \"relation_type\": \"supports\",\n      \"source_claim_id\": null,\n      \"target_claim_id\": null,\n      \"rationale\": \"The learning-deployment workflow explains how compiler decisions can be made by an internal learned model.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"relation_id\": \"supports:claim-the-major-effectiveness-mechanisms-are-eliminating-entries-into-the-middle-of-tr--4bc0ff5e21b0->claim-on-the-benchmark-suite-profile-based-super-block-optimizations-averaged-a-1-15-s--e5d7486c0e56\",\n      \"relation_type\": \"supports\",\n      \"source_claim_id\": null,\n      \"target_claim_id\": null,\n      \"rationale\": \"The identified mechanisms explain why the measured performance improvements can arise.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"relation_id\": \"supports:claim-the-paper-s-worst-case-system-model-uses-one-data-qubit-per-processor-and-a-one--9e5973bc3485->claim-in-the-worst-case-topology-the-entanglement-swapping-based-strategy-has-per-laye--bd58d42b2d90\",\n      \"relation_type\": \"supports\",\n      \"source_claim_id\": null,\n      \"target_claim_id\": null,\n      \"rationale\": \"The entanglement-swapping bound is derived under the stated one-data-qubit linear-nearest-neighbor worst-case architecture.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"relation_id\": \"supports:claim-the-profile-based-transformations-controlled-executable-size-growth-averaging-1--5bacab4b8a28->claim-trace-selection-followed-by-tail-duplication-converts-frequently-executed-traces--1483ee9d0534\",\n      \"relation_type\": \"supports\",\n      \"source_claim_id\": null,\n      \"target_claim_id\": null,\n      \"rationale\": \"Controlled code expansion is evidence that tail duplication can be practical when trace inclusion is thresholded.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"relation_id\": \"supports:claim-thread-coarsening-decisions-are-context-dependent-because-coarsening-can-improve--4878860bda89->claim-direct-prediction-of-the-best-compiler-option-is-practical-for-relatively-small--fe68da808ef3\",\n      \"relation_type\": \"supports\",\n      \"source_claim_id\": null,\n      \"target_claim_id\": null,\n      \"rationale\": \"Thread coarsening is an example of a bounded optimization choice where direct prediction can be useful.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"relation_id\": \"supports:claim-wcc-couples-a-c-compiler-to-the-ait-static-wcet-analyzer-so-that-wcet-data-is-pr--13f9763eb2a9->claim-wcc-s-back-annotation-raises-assembly-level-wcet-information-to-source-level-icd--fc00d3acd6de\",\n      \"relation_type\": \"supports\",\n      \"source_claim_id\": null,\n      \"target_claim_id\": null,\n      \"rationale\": \"Transparent aiT integration supplies the low-level WCET data that back-annotation raises to source-level structures.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"relation_id\": \"supports:claim-wcet-aware-register-allocation-lowers-wcet-by-avoiding-spill-code-on-the-wcep-ev--a21ac879b656->claim-the-wcc-optimizations-compose-applying-register-allocation-code-and-data-scratch--1393cb5b3616\",\n      \"relation_type\": \"supports\",\n      \"source_claim_id\": null,\n      \"target_claim_id\": null,\n      \"rationale\": \"Register allocation is the largest individual component reported in the combined matmult optimization sequence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"relation_id\": \"supports:claim-weighted-flow-graphs-expose-hot-paths-by-attaching-execution-counts-to-basic-blo--49c47f8431d5->claim-execution-profiles-integrated-into-an-optimizing-c-compiler-can-guide-classic-op--20be52b7603e\",\n      \"relation_type\": \"supports\",\n      \"source_claim_id\": null,\n      \"target_claim_id\": null,\n      \"rationale\": \"Weighted execution counts provide the runtime information that lets the compiler focus optimizations on frequently executed regions.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"jq -r '.claims[] | [.source_id, .claim_id, .short_title, .text] | @tsv' verification/example_site/spaces/compilers/outputs/space_overview/subspace--compilers/context.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"jq -r '.claims[] | [.source_id, .claim_id, .short_title, .text] | @tsv' verification/example_site/spaces/compilers/outputs/space_overview/subspace--compilers/context.json\"","aggregated_output":"source-01-using-profile-information-to-assist-classic-code-optimizations--219edcf6f0cf\tclaim-classic-scalar-optimizations-can-be-reformulated-to-operate-on-super-blocks-and--79ce55378df0\tClassic optimizations fit super-blocks\tClassic scalar optimizations can be reformulated to operate on super-blocks and super-block loops rather than only on traditional basic blocks or whole loops.\nsource-02-machine-learning-in-compiler-optimization--5fbaa9c3f69d\tclaim-direct-prediction-of-the-best-compiler-option-is-practical-for-relatively-small--fe68da808ef3\tConstrained choices enable direct prediction\tDirect prediction of the best compiler option is practical for relatively small optimization problems and has produced measurable gains in loop unrolling and thread-coarsening studies.\nsource-03-compiler-design-for-distributed-quantum-computing--64a02810764d\tclaim-distributed-quantum-compilers-must-model-temporal-coupling-map-dynamics-because--0883f72a302d\tCoupling maps become dynamic\tDistributed quantum compilers must model temporal coupling-map dynamics because remote operations are constrained by Bell-state availability, Bell-state regeneration, and classical communication latency.\nsource-03-compiler-design-for-distributed-quantum-computing--64a02810764d\tclaim-distributed-quantum-computing-can-let-remote-quantum-processing-units-cooperate--c8a669f6488f\tDistributed QPUs cooperate virtually\tDistributed quantum computing can let remote quantum processing units cooperate as a virtual quantum processor for tasks that individual noisy intermediate-scale quantum devices cannot handle alone.\nsource-03-compiler-design-for-distributed-quantum-computing--64a02810764d\tclaim-distributed-quantum-computing-requires-compilers-that-can-map-arbitrary-quantum--e4ea92cd41cd\tDistributed architectures require compilers\tDistributed quantum computing requires compilers that can map arbitrary quantum algorithms to distributed architectures while accounting for network and communication constraints.\nsource-05-compiler-aided-systematic-construction-of-large-scale-dna-strand-displacement-circuits--367a566abb69\tclaim-effective-concentration-calibration-guides-thresholds--367a566abb69\tCalibration guides gate thresholds\tEffective concentration calibration provides quantitative threshold choices that restore desired OR and AND gate behavior for unpurified seesaw components.\nsource-03-compiler-design-for-distributed-quantum-computing--64a02810764d\tclaim-entanglement-swapping-augments-distributed-processor-connectivity-by-enabling-re--b0cac39f5fb5\tEntanglement swapping augments connectivity\tEntanglement swapping augments distributed-processor connectivity by enabling remote CNOTs between processors that are not directly connected by a quantum link, but it increases EPR-pair consumption at intermediate processors.\nsource-01-using-profile-information-to-assist-classic-code-optimizations--219edcf6f0cf\tclaim-execution-profiles-integrated-into-an-optimizing-c-compiler-can-guide-classic-op--20be52b7603e\tProfiles guide classic optimizations\tExecution profiles integrated into an optimizing C compiler can guide classic optimizations toward the program regions that run most often.\nsource-03-compiler-design-for-distributed-quantum-computing--64a02810764d\tclaim-experimental-validation-on-medium-size-quantum-circuits-respected-the-analytical--82f1bfd54f5c\tExperiments respect analytical bounds\tExperimental validation on medium-size quantum circuits respected the analytical bounds, and the data-qubit-swapping strategy generally required fewer link-generation layers and lower circuit depth than entanglement swapping alone.\nsource-02-machine-learning-in-compiler-optimization--5fbaa9c3f69d\tclaim-feature-selection-and-dimension-reduction-are-necessary-in-compiler-learning-pro--ecd12a4a4f1f\tFeature reduction preserves signal\tFeature selection and dimension reduction are necessary in compiler-learning problems because larger feature spaces require more training examples and can contain redundant information.\nsource-05-compiler-aided-systematic-construction-of-large-scale-dna-strand-displacement-circuits--367a566abb69\tclaim-full-circuit-recovers-ideal-ca-patterns--367a566abb69\tOutputs match automata patterns\tThe full rule 110-124 DNA circuit produced dual-rail fluorescence outputs at 24 hours that visually matched the intended cellular automata pattern relationships.\nsource-02-machine-learning-in-compiler-optimization--5fbaa9c3f69d\tclaim-future-research-in-machine-learning-compilation-extends-beyond-choosing-optimiza--faf587f1fc17\tOpen questions extend beyond optimization\tFuture research in machine-learning compilation extends beyond choosing optimizations to mapping program and hardware spaces, learning analyses, discovering common features, and possibly learning better intermediate representations.\nsource-04-a-compiler-framework-for-the-reduction-of-worst-case-execution-times--5aee9841160e\tclaim-ilp-based-code-scratchpad-allocation-lowers-wcet-by-moving-beneficial-basic-bloc--d5d88da4e90e\tCode SPM reduces WCET\tILP-based code scratchpad allocation lowers WCET by moving beneficial basic-block regions into fast program scratchpad memory with negligible code-size and solver overhead.\nsource-04-a-compiler-framework-for-the-reduction-of-worst-case-execution-times--5aee9841160e\tclaim-ilp-based-data-scratchpad-allocation-lowers-wcet-by-moving-frequently-accessed-v--8ceca90523fc\tData SPM reduces WCET\tILP-based data scratchpad allocation lowers WCET by moving frequently accessed variables into fast data scratchpad memory without changing generated code size.\nsource-03-compiler-design-for-distributed-quantum-computing--64a02810764d\tclaim-in-the-worst-case-topology-the-entanglement-swapping-based-strategy-has-per-laye--bd58d42b2d90\tEntanglement strategy has linear bound\tIn the worst-case topology, the entanglement-swapping-based strategy has per-layer depth overhead bounded by n/2 times a hardware-dependent constant des, where des equals cle plus cbsm plus ccx.\nsource-04-a-compiler-framework-for-the-reduction-of-worst-case-execution-times--5aee9841160e\tclaim-interprocedural-slicing-and-polyhedral-loop-evaluation-substantially-reduce-loop--8f361a6ac310\tSlicing accelerates loop analysis\tInterprocedural slicing and polyhedral loop evaluation substantially reduce loop-analysis time for many benchmarks while preserving safe loop-bound analysis.\nsource-02-machine-learning-in-compiler-optimization--5fbaa9c3f69d\tclaim-machine-learning-based-compilation-can-make-compiler-optimization-more-evidence--20aeeff3a32c\tEmpirical workflows improve compiler evidence\tMachine-learning-based compilation can make compiler optimization more evidence based because models must be grounded in empirical data that can be tested and independently scrutinized.\nsource-02-machine-learning-in-compiler-optimization--5fbaa9c3f69d\tclaim-machine-learning-based-compilation-can-use-a-model-inside-the-compiler-to-choose--f8131a5c483d\tLearning guides compiler choices\tMachine-learning-based compilation can use a model inside the compiler to choose compiler heuristics or optimizations for a given program according to learned evidence about what makes code faster, smaller, or less power hungry.\nsource-02-machine-learning-in-compiler-optimization--5fbaa9c3f69d\tclaim-machine-learning-based-compiler-optimization-is-limited-by-the-quality-represent--f9c7d385cc26\tTraining data limits learning\tMachine-learning-based compiler optimization is limited by the quality, representativeness, and cost of its training data and cannot by itself create legal transformations or derive legality analyses.\nsource-01-using-profile-information-to-assist-classic-code-optimizations--219edcf6f0cf\tclaim-on-the-benchmark-suite-profile-based-super-block-optimizations-averaged-a-1-15-s--e5d7486c0e56\tProfile optimization speeds benchmarks\tOn the benchmark suite, profile-based super-block optimizations averaged a 1.15 speedup over the prototype compiler's globally optimized code.\nsource-05-compiler-aided-systematic-construction-of-large-scale-dna-strand-displacement-circuits--367a566abb69\tclaim-outlier-gates-expose-synthesis-variation--367a566abb69\tOutliers disrupt gate composition\tGate calibration can identify outlier unpurified components whose effective concentrations differ enough to disrupt multi-layer circuit composition.\nsource-01-using-profile-information-to-assist-classic-code-optimizations--219edcf6f0cf\tclaim-profile-based-classic-optimizations-are-intended-to-complement-conventional-opti--6bcefbcf9607\tProfile optimizations complement convention\tProfile-based classic optimizations are intended to complement conventional optimizations rather than replace them.\nsource-02-machine-learning-in-compiler-optimization--5fbaa9c3f69d\tclaim-program-features-provide-the-quantifiable-representation-that-allows-learning-al--a254f7b701be\tFeatures encode program behavior\tProgram features provide the quantifiable representation that allows learning algorithms to reason about source code, intermediate representation, runtime profiles, or combinations of those properties.\nsource-03-compiler-design-for-distributed-quantum-computing--64a02810764d\tclaim-remote-cnot-execution-consumes-bell-state-resources-and-is-limited-by-the-number--ff11e4d2be8e\tRemote CNOTs consume Bell states\tRemote CNOT execution consumes Bell-state resources and is limited by the number of available communication qubits, creating a tradeoff between communication capacity and data-qubit capacity.\nsource-05-compiler-aided-systematic-construction-of-large-scale-dna-strand-displacement-circuits--367a566abb69\tclaim-rule-110-124-circuit-has-78-species--367a566abb69\tCircuit has 78 species\tThe compiled rule 110-124 DNA strand displacement circuit contains six layers and 78 distinct initial DNA species.\nsource-05-compiler-aided-systematic-construction-of-large-scale-dna-strand-displacement-circuits--367a566abb69\tclaim-seesaw-compiler-automates-dna-circuit-design--367a566abb69\tCompiler automates DNA circuits\tThe Seesaw Compiler automates the translation of feedforward digital logic into equivalent dual-rail and seesaw DNA strand displacement circuits, while producing simulation code and DNA sequences for construction.\nsource-05-compiler-aided-systematic-construction-of-large-scale-dna-strand-displacement-circuits--367a566abb69\tclaim-signal-restoration-compensates-for-impurity--367a566abb69\tRestoration compensates impurity\tSignal restoration and component tuning compensate for impurity in unpurified seesaw circuits, although leak reactions and sensitivity to synthesis and stoichiometry errors remain limiting concerns.\nsource-04-a-compiler-framework-for-the-reduction-of-worst-case-execution-times--5aee9841160e\tclaim-static-wcet-reduction-depends-on-optimizing-the-worst-case-execution-path-becaus--b6a70fae6e3d\tWCEP governs WCET savings\tStatic WCET reduction depends on optimizing the worst-case execution path, because reducing a noncritical path or a local block can leave the global WCET unchanged or only partly reduced.\nsource-01-using-profile-information-to-assist-classic-code-optimizations--219edcf6f0cf\tclaim-super-blocks-represent-frequently-executed-paths-as-linear-basic-block-sequences--7bbb510c9bb0\tSuper-blocks isolate hot paths\tSuper-blocks represent frequently executed paths as linear basic-block sequences that can only be entered at the first block but may exit from any block.\nsource-02-machine-learning-in-compiler-optimization--5fbaa9c3f69d\tclaim-supervised-learning-for-compiler-optimization-learns-correlations-between-progra--217abf25c992\tSupervision maps features to decisions\tSupervised learning for compiler optimization learns correlations between program-feature values and the optimization decisions that produce optimal or near-optimal empirical performance.\nsource-05-compiler-aided-systematic-construction-of-large-scale-dna-strand-displacement-circuits--367a566abb69\tclaim-synthesis-error-model-explains-delayed-outputs--367a566abb69\tError model explains delay\tA model that represents synthesis errors in unpurified molecules predicts the slower 24-hour behavior of the rule 110-124 circuit better than the purified-circuit model.\nsource-05-compiler-aided-systematic-construction-of-large-scale-dna-strand-displacement-circuits--367a566abb69\tclaim-systematic-flow-shortens-unpurified-circuit-building--367a566abb69\tProcedure shortens circuit building\tA three-step systematic procedure of calibration, outlier adjustment, and output tuning enabled construction of the rule 110 sub-circuit in three days.\nsource-01-using-profile-information-to-assist-classic-code-optimizations--219edcf6f0cf\tclaim-tail-duplication-creates-additional-optimization-opportunities-because-it-can-ma--6c81300e0307\tDuplication exposes producer relationships\tTail duplication creates additional optimization opportunities because it can make an earlier operation the sole producer of operands used later in a hot path.\nsource-03-compiler-design-for-distributed-quantum-computing--64a02810764d\tclaim-the-data-qubit-swapping-based-strategy-arranges-data-qubits-so-each-cnot-in-a-la--ba4ebf62d172\tData swapping lowers asymptotic overhead\tThe data-qubit-swapping-based strategy arranges data qubits so each CNOT in a layer operates on neighboring processors, and its compiled per-layer depth does not exceed n/4 dqs plus dqs prime.\nsource-01-using-profile-information-to-assist-classic-code-optimizations--219edcf6f0cf\tclaim-the-experiments-used-separate-profiling-inputs-and-performance-measurement-input--ee5ac2fa5a94\tBenchmarks use separate inputs\tThe experiments used separate profiling inputs and performance-measurement inputs across realistic C application programs.\nsource-01-using-profile-information-to-assist-classic-code-optimizations--219edcf6f0cf\tclaim-the-implementation-cost-of-profile-based-classic-optimization-was-modest-relativ--062df22ec16c\tImplementation cost is modest\tThe implementation cost of profile-based classic optimization was modest relative to the existing global optimizer.\nsource-02-machine-learning-in-compiler-optimization--5fbaa9c3f69d\tclaim-the-machine-learning-compiler-workflow-separates-model-learning-from-deployment--a04ee1ab9738\tTraining precedes deployment\tThe machine-learning compiler workflow separates model learning from deployment: training data is used to learn a model, and the learned model is then inserted into the compiler to make predictions for new programs.\nsource-01-using-profile-information-to-assist-classic-code-optimizations--219edcf6f0cf\tclaim-the-major-effectiveness-mechanisms-are-eliminating-entries-into-the-middle-of-tr--4bc0ff5e21b0\tEffectiveness has two mechanisms\tThe major effectiveness mechanisms are eliminating entries into the middle of traces and optimizing the most frequently executed loop path.\nsource-03-compiler-design-for-distributed-quantum-computing--64a02810764d\tclaim-the-paper-s-worst-case-system-model-uses-one-data-qubit-per-processor-and-a-one--9e5973bc3485\tWorst case maximizes overhead\tThe paper's worst-case system model uses one data qubit per processor and a one-dimensional nearest-neighbor processor topology, making every CNOT remote and maximizing distributed-computation overhead.\nsource-01-using-profile-information-to-assist-classic-code-optimizations--219edcf6f0cf\tclaim-the-profile-based-transformations-controlled-executable-size-growth-averaging-1--5bacab4b8a28\tCode expansion stays controlled\tThe profile-based transformations controlled executable size growth, averaging 1.07 relative size compared with globally optimized programs.\nsource-03-compiler-design-for-distributed-quantum-computing--64a02810764d\tclaim-the-proposed-compiler-is-computationally-efficient-because-distributing-a-circui--b9f318c6234c\tCompiler complexity is polynomial\tThe proposed compiler is computationally efficient because distributing a circuit has O(d n squared) complexity, with d the circuit depth and n the number of QPUs or logical qubits in the modeled worst case.\nsource-04-a-compiler-framework-for-the-reduction-of-worst-case-execution-times--5aee9841160e\tclaim-the-wcc-optimizations-compose-applying-register-allocation-code-and-data-scratch--1393cb5b3616\tOptimizations compose strongly\tThe WCC optimizations compose: applying register allocation, code and data scratchpad allocation, and procedure positioning to matmult reduces WCET by more than 70 percent relative to WCC -O2.\nsource-02-machine-learning-in-compiler-optimization--5fbaa9c3f69d\tclaim-thread-coarsening-decisions-are-context-dependent-because-coarsening-can-improve--4878860bda89\tThread coarsening is context dependent\tThread coarsening decisions are context dependent because coarsening can improve instruction-level parallelism and memory behavior while also reducing parallelism or increasing register pressure on particular programs and hardware.\nsource-01-using-profile-information-to-assist-classic-code-optimizations--219edcf6f0cf\tclaim-trace-selection-followed-by-tail-duplication-converts-frequently-executed-traces--1483ee9d0534\tTail duplication forms super-blocks\tTrace selection followed by tail duplication converts frequently executed traces into super-blocks by removing control-flow entries into the middle of a trace.\nsource-05-compiler-aided-systematic-construction-of-large-scale-dna-strand-displacement-circuits--367a566abb69\tclaim-unpurified-strands-can-build-complex-circuits--367a566abb69\tUnpurified strands support circuits\tUnpurified DNA strands can be used to construct complex DNA strand displacement circuits when circuit design software is combined with simplified experimental procedures.\nsource-04-a-compiler-framework-for-the-reduction-of-worst-case-execution-times--5aee9841160e\tclaim-wcc-couples-a-c-compiler-to-the-ait-static-wcet-analyzer-so-that-wcet-data-is-pr--13f9763eb2a9\tWCC integrates static analysis\tWCC couples a C compiler to the aiT static WCET analyzer so that WCET data is produced transparently during compilation rather than by a separate manual post-compilation step.\nsource-04-a-compiler-framework-for-the-reduction-of-worst-case-execution-times--5aee9841160e\tclaim-wcc-s-back-annotation-raises-assembly-level-wcet-information-to-source-level-icd--fc00d3acd6de\tBack annotation enables optimization\tWCC’s back-annotation raises assembly-level WCET information to source-level ICD-C structures, enabling source-level optimizations to use WCET, WCEP membership, execution frequencies, cache misses, code size, and spill-code data.\nsource-04-a-compiler-framework-for-the-reduction-of-worst-case-execution-times--5aee9841160e\tclaim-wcc-s-loop-analyzer-computes-safe-loop-iteration-bounds-for-most-benchmark-loops--5eb419e33259\tLoop bounds become automatic\tWCC’s loop analyzer computes safe loop iteration bounds for most benchmark loops and exact bounds for the great majority, reducing reliance on manual flow facts.\nsource-04-a-compiler-framework-for-the-reduction-of-worst-case-execution-times--5aee9841160e\tclaim-wcet-aware-procedure-cloning-improves-wcet-estimates-by-specializing-functions-w--808a9c5da846\tCloning sharpens loop bounds\tWCET-aware procedure cloning improves WCET estimates by specializing functions whose data-dependent loop bounds become constant in cloned calling contexts, but it trades timing precision for code-size growth.\nsource-04-a-compiler-framework-for-the-reduction-of-worst-case-execution-times--5aee9841160e\tclaim-wcet-aware-register-allocation-lowers-wcet-by-avoiding-spill-code-on-the-wcep-ev--a21ac879b656\tRegister allocation protects WCEP\tWCET-aware register allocation lowers WCET by avoiding spill code on the WCEP, even when this increases total spill code or text size outside the critical path.\nsource-04-a-compiler-framework-for-the-reduction-of-worst-case-execution-times--5aee9841160e\tclaim-wcet-centric-procedure-positioning-reduces-instruction-cache-conflict-misses-by--47eeb6643a90\tPositioning reduces cache misses\tWCET-centric procedure positioning reduces instruction-cache conflict misses by reordering functions using static WCET-derived call frequencies rather than profiling input data.\nsource-01-using-profile-information-to-assist-classic-code-optimizations--219edcf6f0cf\tclaim-weighted-flow-graphs-expose-hot-paths-by-attaching-execution-counts-to-basic-blo--49c47f8431d5\tWeighted graphs expose hot paths\tWeighted flow graphs expose hot paths by attaching execution counts to basic blocks and taken counts to control-flow arcs.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
